9. SQL MODE
==================================================

Query:

SELECT @@sql_mode;

Explanation:
Shows the current SQL mode.


Output:

ONLY_FULL_GROUP_BY,
STRICT_TRANS_TABLES,
NO_ZERO_IN_DATE,
NO_ZERO_DATE,
ERROR_FOR_DIVISION_BY_ZERO,
NO_ENGINE_SUBSTITUTION


==================================================
10. SESSION SQL MODE
==================================================

Query:

SELECT @@SESSION.sql_mode;

Explanation:
Shows the SQL mode for the current session.


